- summary: |
    HLAfixedRecord composite codec implemented per IEEE 1516.2-2010 §4.
    Per-field padding rule (offset measured from start of record) is
    asserted by explicit byte-layout tests, not just round-trip:
    octet+float64 (7-byte pad), int32+int32 (no pad), int32+float64
    (4-byte pad), and nested record (inner padding resets at inner
    start). The fixed-record-octet-float64 conformance vector is
    enabled (_disabled flag removed) and 3 new fixed-record vectors
    are added under the contiguous "TASK-016 / TASK-017 records"
    block in tests/conformance/encoding_vectors.json.
    Coverage on rti/pkg/encoding/fixed_record.go: ~95% (>= 80%).
- acceptance:
    - fixed-record-octet-float64 vector round-trips byte-identical (placeholder enabled)
    - 3 additional fixed-record vectors with varied padding (no pad, 4-byte pad, nested)
    - explicit byte-layout assertions (not round-trip-only) per §5.5
    - golangci-lint clean on rti/pkg/encoding
    - additive-only on encoding_vectors.json (placeholder enable + appended vectors)
